          "path": "_m/g/c/t/q/st-bees-priory-wp/eight-bells-st-bees-pr.jpg",
          "filename": "St Bees bells in up position.jpg",
          "caption": "The eight bells of St Bees Priory, Cumbria, shown in the \"up\" position, in which they are normally left during rests in a ringing session. When being rung they swing through a full circle from mouth upwards round to mouth upwards, and then swing back again. They are controlled by ropes on full-circle wheels. This method of ringing is know as \"English full-circle bell ringing\". Bells cast in 1857 by Charles and George Mears of Whitechapel.",
          "alt": "The eight bells of St Bees Priory, Cumbria, shown in the \"up\" position, in which they are normally left during rests in a ringing session. When being rung they swing through a full circle from mouth upwards round to mouth upwards, and then swing back again. They are controlled by ropes on full-circle wheels. This method of ringing is know as \"English full-circle bell ringing\". Bells cast in 1857 by Charles and George Mears of Whitechapel.",
